## AI-Assisted Workflow

This repository is set up for plan-then-execute coding: Claude Opus plans each change into `PLAN.md`, a cheaper model executes it one verified step at a time, and any step that needs a decision goes back to Opus. [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is the index of the instructions every agent follows.

{%- if 'claude' in workflow_tools and ('copilot' in workflow_tools or 'local' in workflow_tools) %}

Work in Claude Code or GitHub Copilot, and switch whenever you like: both have the same commands, and `PLAN.md` is the only state they share, so one can plan and the other execute. Each bills its own subscription.
{%- endif %}

| Tool | Plan | Execute | Re-plan one step | Review | Land, then finish |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{%- if 'claude' in workflow_tools %}
| Claude Code | `/plan-feature <what to build>` (or `/plan-bugfix`, `/plan-refactor`, `/plan-tests`, …), or `/plan-issue #42` for an issue, then review `PLAN.md` | `/orchestrate-plan` | `/replan-step N` | `/review-plan-diff` | `/ship-plan`, then `/finish-plan` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'copilot' in workflow_tools %}
| Copilot Chat in VS Code | The Copilot Planner agent on Opus, or `/plan-feature` or `/plan-issue #42` | Run all steps with subagents, or Execute next step | Re-plan with the planner | Review the work | `/ship-plan`, then `/finish-plan` |
| Copilot CLI | `copilot --model claude-opus-5.5`, then `/plan-feature` or `/plan-issue #42` | `/orchestrate-plan` | `/replan-step N` | `/review-plan-diff` | `/ship-plan`, then `/finish-plan` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'local' in workflow_tools %}
| Copilot Chat on the local model | The Hybrid Planner agent on Opus | Run all steps with subagents, or Execute next step, on the shack PC's local model | Re-plan with the planner | Review the work | `/ship-plan`, then `/finish-plan` |
{%- endif %}

{%- if 'claude' in workflow_tools %}

In Claude Code, plan in Accept edits mode and execute in Auto. Each plan gets its own git worktree under `.claude/worktrees/`, so several sessions can work on different plans at once.
{%- endif %}

The workflow files come from a Copier template, which owns them: never edit `.template/`, `.template-version`, `.githooks/commit-msg`, `.github/instructions/project-template.instructions.md`, `.copier-answers.yml`{% if 'claude' in workflow_tools %}, `CLAUDE.md`{% endif %} or the commands, agents and skills the template generates. To change how agents work here, edit `AGENTS.md` or a file it lists. To pull in template improvements, run `.\.template\Update-Project.ps1`: it updates itself, replaces the template's files, merges template changes into the shared settings files, and never touches `AGENTS.md` or this README. To plan the update first, with a trial run, the project files that need changing and the checks, run `/plan-template-update`.
